      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>MADAME MELBA,.</head>
        <p>MADAME MELBA,.</p>
        <p>Madame Melba, who made her reappearance at Covent Garden the other evening, is not only a great singer, but a thoroughly well-informed and accomplished woman .iti other ways, a brilliant conversationalist, and a first-class musician, who can run through a score in MS. or try it over on the piano, on which she is an admirable performer, with equal facility. In London Madame Melba lives in Great Cumberldnd-place, near the Marble Arch, where she has a beautiful house, whose grand saioa was copied from a room in the Palace of Versailles. It is getting on for tweaty years now since Alelha made her, operatic debut as Gilda in "It;goletto" at liruseel FS 1 n 1887. Afteraards she was heard at the Grand Opera, Paris, as Ophelia hi Ambroise Thumas.'s "amulet," and in the following year made her first appearance at Covent i Garden n "Lucia," where her success was immediate.</p>
