      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <head>SELF-RAISING FLOUR The Examiner, Saturday, May 27,</head>
        <p>SELF-RAISING FLOUR The Examiner, Saturday, May 27,</p>
        <p>N'S REALIVL</p>
        <p>DRESS-FASHION HOME.</p>
        <p>'WAnz CRlxowsz!</p>
        <p>'The crinoline war is still waging wordily, and women ire banding themselves together right royally in protest. But I darcsay more good would be done. says 'glebe" in the Genthwoman, if men took some action in tho matter, and formed a league binding themselves to have nothing what- ever to do with women who wore crinolines. This would Surely bring the majority of would-be crinoline wearers to their sense,, though at the same time some men might probably have reason to repent of thfir rashness.</p>
