      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0068" n="art0068">
        <head>Cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People.</head>
        <p>Cured by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People.</p>
        <p>"For five years I suffered untold misery. Whenever I ate, I knew that ten minutes after I should have terrible pains tight through my chest. The headaches I had were fearful. Day by day I grew weaker and weaker, until I had to subsist entirely on milk and weak brandy and water. That was all I could take. My nerves were in iltich a terrible state that 1 couldn't be alone. _ _</p>
        <p>Mrs. Waller, Old House Farm, Eaturst Green, Guild- ford, summed up her case in these words. Mother of fourteen children, the complete breakdown of her Nerves and her fearful state of chronic Indigestion made misery for more than herself. The attack declared itself on a day of mourning. "I could not finish my tea that fateful day. The night before my attack," said she, "I had lost a son, and another one - to - into the hospital</p>
        <p>faller, for five years a sufferer n. _ Nervous Indigestion, was cured by . Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pals Nogio. I went outside the house for a breath of fresh air. I felt stifling. As soon as I got outside I was very sick. The whole evening I feLt to weak and ill to do anything. The attack did not pass off. For nearly five years I suffered untold misery, My husband used to be most anxious about me. I was in such agony at times that I used to scream out."</p>
        <p>! Here evidently was no ordinary case. It is no wonder that ordinary medicine could not cure her. The refusal of the stomach to do its work was not a mere local trouble. The cause was in the brain and nervous system. Chronic nervous dyspepsia thus caused is one of the most obstinate diseases. Dr. William's Pink Pills for Pale People cured Mrs. Waller because they went to the root of the matter, feeding the poor worn-out nerves with rich new blood. Their prompt effects reads like a miracle. "The very first dose seemed to give me relief," she said, "and before I had reached the end of the first box I was nearly well. Fancy that, after nearly five years of agony ! During my long illness I was dispirited, nervous, weak and in pain. But, thanks to Dr. Williams' Pink Pills, I very quickly recovered, and during the three years which have passed since,l have not had any- thing at all the matter with me. So, you see, my cure is permanent." For general breakdown and diseases of the nervous system Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People are invaluable, because they feat the nerves. Hence their wonderful cures in Paralysis, Locomotor Ataxy, Curvature of the Spine and other fatal diseases. Seeing that they are able to cure these, it is not surprising that they easily cure lighter cases as Sciatica, St. Vitus' dance, Neuralgia, and nervous breakdown. For Anternia, Consumption, Indigestion, Rheumatism, and all dis- orders arising from poor or bad blood, and for the troubles that ladies suffer in silence, they are a revela- tion. These pills can be bad at all medicine shops; they are i+ennine if they bear the felt name, Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People. Substitutes are cheaper, but they never cured anyone. Dr. Williams' Medicine Co., Holborn-viaduct, London, send genuine pills post free for Ds. Dd., or six boxes for 1.35. 9d.</p>
