      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-05-27_WidnesExaminer_art0075" n="art0075">
        <head>Tyres and Sunshine.</head>
        <p>Tyres and Sunshine.</p>
        <p>It may not be general known that both the life and elasticity of pneumatic tyres suffer great depreciation when they are exposed 'permanently to strong rays of the sun. When a machine is not iug use it should be kept in a dry place of even temperature and shaded from sunlight. By adopting this plan there is no reason why a bicycle should not last twice the ordinary period of one that does not receive this slight but most necessary attention. One, of course, requires a change of . .</p>
        <p>mount Bometim.cs; but with this little extra' care</p>
        <p>for tyres and mael;ine itself a much better market is found when the time comes for selling it than Would otherwise be the case.</p>
